{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver does not contest that a deviation is established, so the tribunal should spend its time on remedy. The trace EV-GPS-00105 is unbroken — 427 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s — so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and, per POL-RD-01, its figure governs over the rounded trip-record copy: 54.16 km against the 36.0 km booked optimal is an excess of 18.16 km, or 50.44%, which clears both establishment gates and both materiality gates. That being so, the only remedies in play are the arithmetic refund of POL-RD-02 and, if the Judge is satisfied on the profile, the uplift in POL-RD-06(b) — not the whole-fare refund the rider demands.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-GPS-00105",
        "EV-TRIP-00105"
      ],
      "clause_ids": [
        "POL-RD-01",
        "POL-RD-07"
      ],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's account on the file — that PIE traffic was heavy so he took another way — cannot be weighed, and the driver does not ask the tribunal to weigh it. The bundle's only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00105-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and no payload (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT): no advisory names a road or segment the optimal route traverses, and none carries a validity window overlapping the 14:26-15:44 trip. POL-RD-03 is therefore unavailable on this record and, under POL-RD-13, the assertion is tested against the trip's traffic advisory and nothing else. The driver pointed to no advisory ID, so under POL-RD-08 the assertion cites no evidence and carries no weight: the excess stands at the measured figure and no closure-adjusted optimal arises.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-ADVIS-00105-01",
        "EV-CHAT-00105"
      ],
      "clause_ids": [
        "POL-RD-03",
        "POL-RD-08",
        "POL-RD-13"
      ],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The full-fare uplift under POL-RD-06(b) should not be applied here, and I disclose the impairment on which that submission rests. The pattern is carried by a single artifact, EV-DPROF-00105, which is IMPAIRED: issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT, weight 0.75, the snapshot dated 2026-07-11 08:00 being 108 hours before filing against a 72-hour currency threshold and four days BEFORE this trip. The pattern passes only on the absolute limb — deviation_flags_90d of 4 against a threshold of 3 — while the ratio limb is 4/344 = 0.012 against a threshold of 0.05, and the lifetime near-synonym prior_deviation_flags (6) may not be substituted for the 90-day counter that POL-RD-06 names (POL-GEN-01 forbids the substitution). Under POL-GEN-02(2) confidence in a fact carried solely by that artifact is capped at 0.75, and under POL-GEN-02(3) the Judge must name the artifact, its weight and its issue codes; a 43.33 SGD uplift (65.13 charged against the 21.80 POL-RD-02 refund) should not be built on a stale, pre-trip, down-weighted snapshot. The driver's rating, acceptance rate, lifetime trips, cancellation rate and active region are context only under POL-GEN-01 and cannot carry any finding.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-DPROF-00105",
        "EV-GPS-00105"
      ],
      "clause_ids": [
        "POL-RD-06",
        "POL-GEN-01",
        "POL-GEN-02"
      ],
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "Declining the uplift, the remedy is fixed arithmetic and the rider's demand for the whole fare is not a licensed one. Recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 36.0 km + 0.28 x 42.0 min) x 1.0 surge, + 0.80 platform fee = 43.36; the refund is 65.13 - 43.36 = 21.77, rounded up to 21.80, which is 33.4% of the charged total and far short of the 90% that would convert a partial refund into a full one. The rider asks for the entire fare and expressly 'not a partial adjustment', but POL-RD-02 makes the refund arithmetic rather than discretionary, and POL-GEN-03 returns the whole contested amount only where the filing party is entirely right.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-FARE-00105",
        "EV-TRIP-00105"
      ],
      "clause_ids": [
        "POL-RD-02",
        "POL-GEN-03"
      ],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing may be added on top of that figure. The fare carries no ERP or toll lines at all — erp_gantries is empty and tolls_erp is 0.00 — and no airport surcharge (airport_surcharge 0.00, correctly so, because a Changi surcharge attaches only to trips ORIGINATING at the airport and this trip terminates there). POL-RD-09(1)'s anti-double-count rule therefore leaves no off-route pass-through to itemise, and POL-RD-09(4) has no phantom gantry or surcharge line to refund. The surge multiplier was read from the fare_breakdown (1.0), not from the trip record, and surge_amount is 0.00, so no surge uplift inflates the recomputation.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-FARE-00105"
      ],
      "clause_ids": [
        "POL-RD-09",
        "POL-RD-02"
      ],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The contested sum is the published rate card applied to the distance and time actually driven, not a penalty or a discretionary charge that could be stripped out beyond the recomputation: 3.80 base + 40.65 distance (54.2 km at 0.75) + 19.88 time (71 min at 0.28) + 0.80 platform fee = 65.13, with no surge, toll, waiting or premium line anywhere in the breakdown. There is accordingly no billing-integrity defect under POL-RD-09(4) and nothing in this fare that the driver should be made to give back beyond the POL-RD-02 arithmetic.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-FARE-00105",
        "EV-TRIP-00105"
      ],
      "clause_ids": [
        "POL-RD-02",
        "POL-RD-09"
      ],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's narrative of nearly missing check-in does not enlarge the remedy. The rider's own message in the chat log puts the flight at 17:15, and the trip record shows the vehicle reaching the dropoff at 15:44:05; no artifact on the file records a missed or nearly missed check-in, and the driver's own statement on the record is that the passenger reached the airport in time. Inconvenience is not a head of relief in this vocabulary — POL-RD-02 gives arithmetic and POL-GEN-03 gives the whole contested amount only where the claim is fully made out — so the timing narrative supports neither the whole-fare demand nor any sum beyond the recomputation.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-CHAT-00105",
        "EV-TRIP-00105"
      ],
      "clause_ids": [
        "POL-RD-02",
        "POL-GEN-03"
      ],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 65.13,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c): refer the case to driver-conduct review — a repeat deviation pattern (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 4 on EV-DPROF-00105) is established alongside a material, substantiated deviation on this trip (EV-GPS-00105). The referral rides with the refund and does not displace or delay it."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.75,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the driver took a materially longer route and I am refunding the whole SGD 65.13 that was charged.\n\nROUTE. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00105 is complete — 427 fixes at 10-second intervals, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s — so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and its figure governs over the rounded trip-record copy (POL-RD-01). It records 54.16 km driven against the 36.0 km booked optimal on EV-TRIP-00105: an excess of 18.16 km, or 50.44%. That clears both establishment gates and both materiality gates of POL-RD-01, so the deviation is ESTABLISHED and MATERIAL. The rider's measurement claim is accepted and the driver does not contest it.\n\nEXCULPATION. None runs. The driver's statement that PIE traffic was heavy is unsupported by any traffic advisory. The bundle's only advisory, EV-ADVIS-00105-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and no payload (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT). The driver names no advisory ID, so under POL-RD-13(1) the missing advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction in it and does not escalate under POL-RD-10(5); under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13(2) the uncited assertion carries no weight and the excess stands at the measured figure. POL-RD-03 is unavailable on this record. POL-RD-04 finds no rider instruction to detour in the chat log (EV-CHAT-00105); POL-RD-05 finds no amended pickup or dropoff; POL-RD-12 does not apply (vehicle_type RYDE_X, not pooled).\n\nTHE POL-RD-02 FIGURE. (Base fare 3.80 + 0.75 x 36.0 km + 0.28 x 42.0 min) x surge 1.0, read from EV-FARE-00105, the only artifact carrying the multiplier + platform fee 0.80 = recomputed_fare 43.36. Charged_total on EV-FARE-00105 is 65.13. Refund = 65.13 - 43.36 = 21.77, rounded up to 21.80 — 33.4% of the charge, below the 90% full-refund share. The driver's claim that the remedy is fixed at this figure is accepted as the POL-RD-02 figure and rejected as the final remedy, for the reason below.\n\nTHE POL-RD-06 UPLIFT. A MATERIAL deviation requires the driver-profile check, and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d on EV-DPROF-00105 is 4, at or above the clause's threshold of 3; the repeat pattern is ESTABLISHED. The test is disjunctive, so the driver's point that the ratio limb (4/344 = 0.012) falls short does not help him, and prior_deviation_flags (6) is a lifetime counter that POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting for the 90-day figure. EV-DPROF-00105 is impaired — issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT, weight_multiplier 0.75, its snapshot dated 108 hours before filing against a 72-hour currency threshold and four days before this trip — and I name that impairment here as POL-GEN-02(3) requires; the 4-against-3 finding survives the discount. Because the deviation is also MATERIAL and substantiated on this trip's own trace, POL-RD-06(b) replaces the POL-RD-02 partial with FULL_REFUND of charged_total. Side by side, as the clause requires: POL-RD-02 partial 21.80; POL-RD-06(b) uplifted figure 65.13. There is no government-set or third-party pass-through line to carve out — EV-FARE-00105 shows no ERP, no tolls and no airport surcharge (the Changi surcharge attaches only to trips ORIGINATING at an airport and this trip terminates there) — so the whole 65.13 is refunded.\n\nPOL-RD-09. No ERP or toll lines and no surcharge line, so there is nothing to itemise, no double-count risk under limb (1), and no billing-integrity defect under limb (4) for either side.\n\nTHE RIDER'S NARRATIVE. The rider is refunded the whole fare, but not because check-in was nearly missed: inconvenience is not a head of relief in this vocabulary and no artifact records a missed or nearly missed check-in, so that part of the claim adds nothing to the remedy.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND ESCALATION. My confidence is capped at 0.75 under POL-GEN-02(2), the weight of EV-DPROF-00105, the only artifact carrying the repeat-pattern fact the uplift rests on. That is at or above the 0.70 confidence floor read from the loaded policy, so the case is decided rather than escalated; I have run each POL-RD-10 trigger and none fires. This ruling differs from precedents P-0001 and P-0002, which share POL-RD-01, POL-RD-02 and POL-RD-08 but carried no POL-RD-06 repeat-pattern finding: it is that finding on EV-DPROF-00105 that lifts this case from a partial to a full refund.\n\nEXECUTION. The monetary effect, 65.13, exceeds the POL-GEN-05 threshold of 8.00, so this provisional ruling issues but the amount is held for release by a human reviewer. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The driver's only explanation is that traffic was heavy on the PIE. No LTA advisory covering the 14:26-15:44 trip window is on file: EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0. Under POL-RD-13 an external-traffic excuse is tested against the traffic_advisory and nothing else; that comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and under POL-RD-08 the assertion carries no weight. Because the driver names no advisory identifier at all, this is a gap in the bundle rather than a conflict in it, so the absence does not escalate under POL-RD-10(5). The deviation therefore stands at the measured 18.16 km and POL-RD-02 runs against the booked 36.0 km optimal.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00105-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 65.13,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c): refer driver DRV-00932 to driver-conduct review for the established repeat deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d = 4, against a threshold of 3), the pattern finding resting on EV-DPROF-00105 (STALE_SNAPSHOT, weight 0.75)."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.75,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the measurement is common ground and I adopt it. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00105 (weight 1.0, no admissibility issue; 427 fixes at 10-second intervals, 100% coverage, zero gaps) governs distance under POL-RD-01: 54.16 km trace against the booked optimal of 36.0 km on EV-TRIP-00105, an excess of 18.16 km, or 50.4%. That passes both establishment gates (20% / 0.8 km) and both materiality gates (50% / 8.0 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED and MATERIAL. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a) to (c), so no independent corroboration is required and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises. No exculpatory clause runs: there is no rider instruction in EV-CHAT-00105 (POL-RD-04 unavailable), no amended endpoint on EV-TRIP-00105 (POL-RD-05 unavailable), and vehicle_type RYDE_X (POL-RD-12 unavailable).\n\nThe driver's traffic explanation carries nothing. The bundle holds no traffic advisory for the trip window: EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. The driver named no advisory ID, so under POL-RD-13 this is a gap in the bundle rather than the conflict POL-RD-10(5) escalates, and under POL-RD-08 a bare assertion that traffic was bad discharges no burden. POL-RD-03 is unavailable. The deviation therefore stands at the measured 18.16 km with POL-RD-02 running against the booked 36.0 km optimal.\n\nRemedy. The POL-RD-02 arithmetic is not in dispute: (3.80 base + 0.75 x 36.0 km + 0.28 x 42.0 min) x the 1.0 surge multiplier read from EV-FARE-00105 (the only artifact carrying that field) + 0.80 platform fee = 43.36 recomputed_fare. charged_total 65.13 less 43.36 = 21.77, rounded up to 21.80. At 33.4% of charged_total that alone would be a PARTIAL_REFUND of 21.80, and the rider's demand for a flat whole-fare refund is not granted on that footing.\n\nBut the POL-RD-06(b) uplift does apply. The deviation is both material and substantiated on this trip's own evidence, and the repeat pattern is ESTABLISHED because driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 4 against the clause's threshold of 3. I accept the driver's disclosure that EV-DPROF-00105 is IMPAIRED: issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT, weight_multiplier 0.75, its snapshot of 2026-07-11 08:00 being stale against the 2026-07-15 trip and filing. Under POL-GEN-02 the finding survives that discount: it passes on the absolute limb (4 >= 3) even though the ratio limb does not (4/344 = 0.012 < 0.05), and the lifetime near-synonym prior_deviation_flags (6) is not used, as POL-GEN-01 requires. The driver's submission that the uplift should be refused is rejected: staleness down-weights the pattern's confidence, it does not fail the test the clause states. The impairment caps my confidence in the uplift at 0.75, which is above the 0.70 floor, so the uplift is applied rather than withheld.\n\nPOL-RD-06(b) therefore gives FULL_REFUND of charged_total: 65.13, against the POL-RD-02 figure of 21.80, an uplift of 43.33, printed here so its size is auditable. There are no government-set or third-party pass-through lines to carve out (ERP 0.00, tolls 0.00, airport surcharge 0.00, correctly zero because the Changi surcharge attaches only to trips ORIGINATING at the airport and this trip terminates there), so nothing is settled separately under POL-RD-09 and there is no billing-integrity defect. The rider's near-missed check-in narrative is not itself a head of relief and neither enlarges nor reduces the sum; the full refund comes from POL-RD-06(b). The chat log corroborates the rider's account of the route, but the unbroken trace needs no such corroboration.\n\nReferral: under POL-RD-06(c) the case is referred to driver-conduct review; that referral rides with the money and does not delay it. Confidence 0.75. The money moves and exceeds the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the amount is held for release under POL-GEN-05, and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04. This ruling differs from precedents P-0001 and P-0002 only in that those cases carried no established POL-RD-06 repeat pattern, whereas here deviation_flags_90d of 4 engages the POL-RD-06(b) uplift."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The driver's only explanation is that traffic was heavy on the PIE. No LTA advisory covering the 14:26-15:44 trip window is on file: EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0. Under POL-RD-13 an external-traffic excuse is tested against the traffic_advisory and nothing else; that comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and under POL-RD-08 the assertion carries no weight. Because the driver names no advisory identifier at all, this is a gap in the bundle rather than a conflict in it, so the absence does not escalate under POL-RD-10(5). The deviation therefore stands at the measured 18.16 km and POL-RD-02 runs against the booked 36.0 km optimal.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00105-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
